WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.870
Meeting in progress

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.590
Well then, I will take attendance before the meeting starts.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.590
- Igusa.
- Here.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.060
- Tayune.
- Here.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.620
- Gokyoya.
- Here.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.130
Tensou.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.360
Tensou?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.560
Yes, here.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.400
- Furano.
- Here, here.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.730
Imari and Sayoka.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:38.870
Here.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.570
- Tomohane.
- Yes, here.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.340
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.680
That means...

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:54.350
Geez, why does that girl keep showing up late?

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.890
Excuse me. Sorry for being late.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:02.760
Nadeshiko.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.730
It seems that you don't understand the meaning of teamwork.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.540
I'm sorry, I was receiving a call from Master Kaoru.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.340
What?

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.270
From Master Kaoru?

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.810
Why is it always only you?

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.750
Very well. Take your seat, quickly.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.180
Yes, forgive me.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:32.560
Now then, the client for this job is my older brother.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.490
From Hake?

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.420
- What's it about?
- Be quiet.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.760
I'm explaining it now.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.800
To be exact, I've received a request from Master Kaoru.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.070
Brother?

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.340
This is the message from Master Kaoru.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.900
Master Kaoru

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.340
"Do the next job on your own."
Master Kaoru

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:52.910
Master Kaoru

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.340
"I'm counting on everyone."
Master Kaoru

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.550
- Understood.
- Leave it to us.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.850
I'll do my best.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.380
And I'm house-sitting for this mission.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.850
How unlucky.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.360
Gokyoya, got the short straw.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.860
Please work hard for my part too.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.090
Umm, Sendan.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.630
What is it?

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.370
Can I stay home too?

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.500
What did you say?

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.340
Nadeshiko, you always say that.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.640
Stop it, Tayune.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.240
There it is again, the reluctant Nadeshiko.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.880
She always stays home.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.880
Very well, do as you wish.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.520
That'll make it easier to do our job anyway.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.090
Thank you, Sendan.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.930
To make sure we meet
Master Kaoru's trust in us,

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.930
we will need to make sure this job is successful, no matter what.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.100
We, as Master Kaoru's Inukami,

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.800
shall go with our hearts united as one.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.000
Understood!

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.550
<i>Can I keep on praying?</i>

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.850
<i>Can I keep on believing?</i>

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:13.760
<i>Oh light that shines</i> <i>in the forest of despair</i>

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:30.270
<i>I kick the cold ground with my toes</i>

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:37.150
<i>My brushed hair</i> <i>dances in the moonlit night</i>

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:43.950
<i>Let's throw away your</i> <i>frightened eyes and loneliness</i>

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:51.760
<i>Those days when acting tough</i> <i>was your only friend...</i>

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.300
<i>Leave that in the distance</i>

00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:00.240
<i>Is my salvation over there?</i>

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.470
<i>Can I heal this deep darkness?</i>

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:09.210
<i>Is it okay for me to seek warmth?</i>

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.620
<i>I want to be stronger</i> <i>than anyone else</i>

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.920
<i>I want to protect my loved ones</i>

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:22.960
<i>Oh light that continues</i> <i>to shine on me</i>

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.930
Exterminating in Swimsuits!

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:29.000
"Exterminating in Swimsuits!"

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.210
Well, how should I say this...

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.850
She found some dirty magazines under the bed and went nuts.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.590
It's not a big deal, right?

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.490
Now they're all prohibited ever since Yoko came.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.190
Wait just a little bit, okay?

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.770
Normally, you'd cook after you clean up.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.940
She can't do such basic things like that.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.170
I see.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:13.210
It's not like I'm asking for lot.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.380
I just wanted an Inukami

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.080
that can do housework and is somewhat obedient.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.550
That's all I ever wanted.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.790
Here you go, Keita.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.730
See?

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.470
Yoko, do you have any intention to ever cook?

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:39.700
Well, it's tastier when you're the one cooking.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.840
How about cleaning up the room?

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.370
But it's way tidier when you clean.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.510
Shouldn't you at least clean up your own mess?

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.380
But it's your own fault in the first place.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.120
Because you were hiding this from me.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.150
There we go.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:58.390
My Yukari!

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.390
Well then, let's eat!

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:04.560
What do you think?

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:09.100
Indeed. For an Inukami, this is troublesome.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.470
What? What are you guys talking about?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.240
You stay out of this.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.540
Now then, for our current job...

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.240
We are asked to exterminate

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.310
the suspicious spirit that appears in the Water Garden indoor swimming pool.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.120
I know that place.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.390
They just opened recently, right?

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.190
Yes, but apparently,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.590
spiritual phenomena have occurred since it opened.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.890
Oh my, that sure is trouble.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:39.730
Yay! We have the whole pool to ourselves!

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.430
Tomohane, we're here for work.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.900
Then, what are we supposed to do?

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.100
Yeah, what?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:49.140
First, we act like normal customers and look for the enemy.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.370
Then, exterminate it.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:55.010
Please refrain from acting on your own. Understood?

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.550
Yes.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:02.890
Well, where could it be hiding?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.790
Come on, Keita. Hurry up.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:11.390
"Hurry up"? They're closed today.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.470
How is it? Feeling excited now?

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.840
Yes...

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.670
Yes, yes...

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.710
- Telep...
- Yay.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.010
Viva pool!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.450
Viva swimsuits.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.780
Viva girls' bodies.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.520
Yippee!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.990
Buzz off, pervert.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:48.660
Oh, I was wondering what kind of demon you were.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.800
Turns out it's just you, Yoko.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.670
Oh, I thought I've seen your faces.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:57.610
It's the coward Inukami that can't do anything without all ten.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.510
What did you say?

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:01.780
Oh, my bad. There's only eight of you today,

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.810
so you'll achieve even less.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.950
That's enough with the greetings.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:10.290
So why are you here today?

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:11.590
It's a job.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:15.260
We were hired to exterminate something weird at this pool.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.190
What did you say?

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:18.560
Then it's the same as our job.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.270
Igusa, behind you!

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.840
What's this? My clothes are melting.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.820
Calm down. And you say you're Master Kaoru's Inukami?

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.620
How shameful when there are eight of you.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.520
- Yoko, let's go.
- Right.

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.420
In the name of the wise Hakusan.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.430
Frog, burn!

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.270
Yoko, now.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.030
I got this!

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.040
Evil Blaze.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.430
It's over, Keita...

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:29.970
So, you guys are Kaoru's Inukami?
I'm Kaoru's cousin, Keita Kawahira.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.770
Nice to meet you.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:35.300
Hey, you two over there.
You're twins?

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:40.580
Oh come on, let's get along.
Let's start by becoming friends.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.910
Okay? Friends...

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:48.620
Keita.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.650
No, I was just thinking

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:54.620
about getting closer with my cousin's Inukami...

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.130
There is no need.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:02.130
Evil Blaze!

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:28.020
"Inukami!"

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:32.460
I see. Both of you got the same job.

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:36.430
It was a personal request from the pool's owner.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.200
I should've reconfirmed it.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.140
It's not your fault, it's just a small mistake.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:45.810
But I'm pretty sure those girls won't be satisfied.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:47.510
- Sir.
- Yes?

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.910
What is the meaning of this?

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:52.980
Why is there another
Inukami besides us?

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:57.550
That's my line. I mean, we were requested personally by you.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.760
Um, that's... How should I say it.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.530
Spit it out. You were two-timing us!

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.530
That is so cruel.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.900
This is just too much.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:10.230
That's right.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.230
I'll curse you.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.770
- It's fraud!
- It's totally fraud.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:21.010
I'm sorry. I just wanted this matter to be resolved as soon as possible.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:25.010
So are you saying that you couldn't trust us?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.320
Well, it's not like
I couldn't understand that.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.420
What?

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:32.790
But the eight of you couldn't do anything.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:35.360
Meanwhile, I took care of it alone.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.890
Umm... Sorry but...

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:39.800
It's really hard to say this,

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.430
but I called you by mistake.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:48.640
When I called again, they gave me the same "Kawahira" name.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.170
So I accidentally called
Mister Keita too.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:12:00.120
Now it's clear who's the unwanted guest here.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.690
Shut up!

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:08.160
But I defeated the enemy.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.630
You're all still incompetent.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:11.990
What?

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:13.200
You want to fight?

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.970
Fighting, as expected.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:21.540
My apologies. Those girls are very diligent about work.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.870
It's okay. But more importantly...

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.840
About Yoko...

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:31.350
With Yoko's case, I think taking physical action is also an option.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.580
You mean by force? That's impossible.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:37.050
If anything, I'm the one getting all the beatings.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:38.320
You know, right?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:42.360
I spent more nights in jail than in my own house this month.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:44.430
Well that's...

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.030
What if...

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:46.900
Master Keita?

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.900
Never mind, I'm asking too much.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:54.900
I guess I have no other choice but to endure these hellish, violent days.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.770
- Master Keita.
- Curious?

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.510
Want to know what I'm thinking?

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:01.780
Yes, I guess.

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:03.510
Give her a role model.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:07.850
In other words, borrow an Inukami from somewhere that can

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:11.020
do chores, is smart, and most importantly, obedient.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:13.790
Where do you mean by "somewhere"?

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:16.120
I'm leaving that part to you.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.260
Anyway, I want to use an honor student-like role model.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:23.300
After that, Yoko might just follow her example.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:29.370
Oh. If possible, I'd like a really cute female Inukami.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:30.310
Why?

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.780
Why? Well if she at least looks as good as Yoko,

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.380
Yoko will pay attention.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.710
I see.

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:38.310
Understood.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.920
I will report this to my master.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.120
Really?

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.490
Yes. As expected of Master Keita, it's a good idea.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.560
Well then, I will be going.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:53.730
Keita.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.460
- We're going home.
- Ouch.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.300
Done talking?

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.600
Pretty much.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.840
Well then Sendan, that's it.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:01.970
Now wait a minute.

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.970
Why aren't you taking the payment?

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.710
No big reason.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.280
I'm giving it to you because I don't want it.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.650
What? Yoko, are you serious?

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:15.380
No way I'm accepting money for a job we got by accident.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.250
You 10 buddies split it.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.450
What did you say?

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.160
You want to fight me?

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.830
Really, you're all fools.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.430
The only decent one is Nadeshiko.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.570
Next time you come out, bring her too.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.200
Then maybe I'll play with you.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.340
- Farewell...
- Hey, Yoko.

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:38.170
Don't decide alone!

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:41.610
Without this pay, they'll stop our electricity again!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.280
Gas and water too.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.650
And it's not like this job is over.

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:47.380
Shut up!

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.290
You stupid mutt!

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.620
Everyone, we're going home.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.060
Umm.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:58.990
Huh?

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:01.600
There's something bothering me.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.030
What did you say?

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:09.040
No, I'm just saying that there's a possibility.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.570
What do you mean?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:13.140
You evaporated the enemy with Evil Blaze.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:17.310
But once steam cools down, it'll turn back to water.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.650
Then the enemy might be...

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:23.120
If you knew that, why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.120
I'll be ridiculed again!

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.160
Keita, you idiot!

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:31.760
I tried to tell you back then, didn't I? But you...

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.960
Geez. Keita, you idiot!

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:35.100
Don't!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.600
This time it's Midori.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:39.630
I don't care.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:44.440
That's why, I think the enemy might still be around.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:48.710
Indeed, the possibility is pretty high.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:52.950
But if that were the case, to completely take out the enemy,

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:57.120
we'll need a power stronger than Yoko's Evil Blaze.

00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:58.790
Wait, you don't mean...

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.860
Purgatory.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:03.160
I understand.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.790
Contact Gokyoya and everyone.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:11.800
So basically, we need the power of all ten of us for this plan to work.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.170
Together, we shall unite our hearts as one.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:17.510
Um... I'm not good at fighting.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.810
You always refuse to fight.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.980
We are fighting against evils that harm humans.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:30.390
But, we could also move them to a place without humans.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.220
I think we could resolve it by talking.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:37.860
So you don't wish to resolve it by force.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:42.330
It sounds persuasive when you say it.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.440
Above.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.410
My favorite clothes!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.650
No, help us!

